{
 "test": "reader_phase",
 "what": "On the same w00 surface of PHerc0841's known-text region, how much of the 2.4 um reader's letter-shape signal does the public 9.6 um reader (Hecate 9.6) keep, and does that share depend on where each reader's tiles start?",
 "measure": "Both readers' ink maps are put on one 9.6 um grid. Each map is band-pass filtered (difference of Gaussians, sigma 1.5 px minus sigma 12 px) and compared window by window (128 px windows, step 64) with the organizers' 2.4 um ink prediction for this segment, filtered the same way (Pearson r). Only windows with >= 5 % of the prediction above its Otsu threshold count. 'Good' windows are those where the 2.4 um reader's r is >= 0.5 and in its top third (chosen again for each 2.4 um tile phase; < 10 good windows makes that phase VOID). The number per pair is the median over good windows of r(9.6 um reader) / r(2.4 um reader). The reference prediction comes from the same 2.4 um scan as the 2.4 um reader, so the measure favours the 2.4 um reader; the 9.6 um reader may have been distilled on this scroll, which favours it. A ratio is conditional on the frozen CT registration shift.",
 "phases": {
  "T": "2.4 um reader (Hecate 2.4): leading margins (my, mx) in {0,32,64,96}^2 px at 2.403 um (stride 128)",
  "H9": "9.6 um reader (Hecate 9.6): leading margins (my, mx) in {40,48,56,64}^2 px at 9.6 um (stride 32)",
  "pair_key": "'T<my>,<mx>|H<my>,<mx>'; 16 x 16 = 256 pairs per region"
 },
 "class_rule": {
  "reader_limited": "median ratio <= 0.60",
  "surface_candidate": "median ratio >= 0.85",
  "mixed": "in between"
 },
 "outcome_rule": "Per region: VOID if more than 4 of 16 T phases are VOID; CLASS-STABLE <class> if every valid pair falls in the same class; PHASE-DEPENDENT if any two valid pairs disagree (no 90 % rule). Headline = R2's outcome.",
 "t_phase_rule": "For each H9 phase, the range (max - min) over the T phases; then the median over the 16 H9 phases. T-PHASE-MATERIAL if > 0.10, T-PHASE-MINOR if <= 0.05, otherwise reported. The H9-phase effect is the mirror: for each T phase the range over H9 phases, median over T phases (the Judge's definition).",
 "void_note": "Per-pair good-window counts were not saved; VOID is applied from the job's void_T_phases list (empty for both regions).",
 "rounding_note": "The job reported R2's H9-phase effect as 0.175: it took the median of ranges that were already rounded to 3 decimals. The Judge recomputed from the 256 stored ratios (unrounded ranges): 0.176. The release code uses the Judge's definition.",
